# Quality and security rules

- Validate untrusted input at boundaries with runtime schemas.
- Default deny. Authorize every sensitive operation server-side.
- Add positive and negative authorization tests, especially cross-tenant tests.
- Add regression tests for bug fixes and tests for state transitions.
- Never weaken tests just to make CI pass.
- Do not log secrets, tokens, full private manuscripts, reviewer identities in blinded workflows, or sensitive payloads.
- Do not expose private manuscript/review/proof files via permanent public URLs.
- Report exactly which checks were run and which were not.
